rust/target/

# Build-context stability. CI clones this fork fresh for every run, so the
# root .git tree (FETCH_HEAD, reflogs, pack checksums) differs byte-for-byte
# even when the commit is identical. With it in the context the
# `COPY . /src/vllm` layer digest changed every build and invalidated the
# ~3h of CUDA compile layers underneath it. The commit and the
# setuptools-scm version are passed as build args instead
# (VLLM_SOURCE_COMMIT / VLLM_SCM_VERSION).
.git
.github

# CI definitions are never read by the build, and the sanctioned way to force a
# rebuild is a comment bump in .tekton/spark-build-on-push.yaml (pathChanged is
# the PAC trigger). With .tekton in the context that bump changed the
# `COPY . /src/vllm` digest, so every deliberate retrigger threw away the whole
# ~3h CUDA compile -- the exact opposite of what a retrigger should cost.
.tekton

# Never read by the wheel build (packaging is `include = ["vllm*"]`), but large
# enough to slow the context upload and to invalidate the CUDA compile layers on
# doc-only or test-only commits.
tests
docs
examples
benchmarks

.logs
